    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="Panzergrenadier Squad" hidden="false" id="be41-c2c4-ade9-66d0">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="d42d-87f6-d04b-43db" id="ba1d-fe8c-82dd-8390" primary="true" name="Infantry" />
        <categoryLink targetId="9e10-0000-0000-0002" id="015e-591d-f17e-e03b" primary="false" name="Period: Mid War" />
        <categoryLink targetId="9e10-0000-0000-0003" id="d3d4-8365-d0b8-c96e" primary="false" name="Period: Late War" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Hitler's Buzz-Saw" hidden="false" type="rule" id="1b29-914b-6b18-eae9" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0001" />
        <infoLink name="Initiative Training" hidden="false" type="rule" id="befe-3b14-c519-9610" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0003" />
        <infoLink name="Defend the Fatherland!" hidden="false" type="rule" id="9520-82b4-733d-6e4f" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0005" />
      </infoLinks>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Panzergrenadier Squad" hidden="false" id="ba2b-db86-08d7-5b2c" typeId="9b00-0000-0000-0001" typeName="Army Book Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Period" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0001">M/L</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Composition / Type" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0002">1 NCO and 4 men</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Weapons" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0003">Rifles</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Rules and options" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0004">Mechanised infantry: Panzergrenadier squads can re-roll any failed order test that is required to mount or dismount a transport vehicle. In addition, if their transport vehicle is destroyed, Panzergrenadier units suffer D3 hits rather than D6 hits.; Tank hunters (if anti-tank grenades taken); Defend the Fatherland! (if taken) Panzerfaust Seeking a cheap, effective anti-tank weapon with which to arm their infantry, Germany developed the Panzerfaust (tr. ‘Armour Fist’). A simple one- shot weapon, the Panzerfaust utilised a shaped charge warhead capable of significant armour penetration, albeit at short range, and starting in 1943 would be produced in the millions over two main variants. A lethal weapon, particularly in urban environments or similar dense terrain, it would pave the way for the infantry light anti-tank weapons of today, and proved an exceptionally useful force multiplier for the Wehrmacht. Many would be issued to Germany’s last-ditch forces in the closing stages of the war, and many more would see service after being captured by Germany’s enemies, such was their recognised value in combat.; Add up to 5 men with rifles at +11pts (regular) or +14pts (veteran) each; The NCO and up to 3 men may replace their rifles with submachine guns for +4pts each; The NCO and up to 4 other men may replace their rifles with assault rifles for +6pts eac; Up to 2 men may replace their rifle with a light machine gun for +15pts each - for each light machine gun included another man becomes the loader.; Up to 4 men may have a panzerfaust in addition to other weapons for +15pts each; The squad may be given anti-tank grenades for +2pts per figure; Defend the Fatherland! (Waffen-SS); If taken as Waffen-SS any man may replace their rifle with an assault rifle for +6pts</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Army Book" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0005">p. 31</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Experience" id="0e6c-281b-5083-0c97">
