        <infoLink name="Panzer Ace" hidden="false" type="rule" id="59a0-0394-324f-322d" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0004" />
      </infoLinks>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Ferdinand And Elefant" hidden="false" id="00ff-c93c-ae31-0780" typeId="9b00-0000-0000-0001" typeName="Army Book Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Period" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0001">M/L</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Composition / Type" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0002">11+ (super-heavy tank)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Weapons" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0003">1 casement-mounted forward-facing super-heavy anti-tank gun</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Rules and options" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0004">given below. Although production was limited to a single run of under a hundred vehicles, almost all of which were completed in 1943, Ferdinand equipped units continued to fight on the Russian Front and in Italy until the end of the war. Half of all vehicles built were lost at the battle of Kursk in 1943, mostly immobilised by mines and then destroyed with magnetic anti-tank mines, after which the survivors were modified to include a defensive machine gun - this final variant was known as the Elefant (‘Elephant’). Principal service: 1943- 45. Numbers manufactured: 90. Cost 304pts (Inexperienced), 380pts (Regular), 456pts (Veteran) Weapons 1 casement-mounted forward-facing super-heavy anti-tank gun damage Value 11+ (super-heavy tank) Options; Add 1 forward-facing hull-mounted MMG (Elefant) for +10pts Special Rules; Panzer Ace; Slow; Unreliable; Add 1 forward-facing hull-mounted MMG (Elefant) for +10pts</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Army Book" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0005">p. 67</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
