    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="Borgward B-IV Demolition Vehicle" hidden="false" id="3862-689b-e6f3-4c43">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="6912-835d-246f-48a2" id="74e5-76bb-20ab-5894" primary="true" name="Armour" />
        <categoryLink targetId="9e10-0000-0000-0002" id="20fe-13d9-51b3-b6e5" primary="false" name="Period: Mid War" />
        <categoryLink targetId="9e10-0000-0000-0003" id="2ec7-ec0c-4598-8546" primary="false" name="Period: Late War" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Hitler's Buzz-Saw" hidden="false" type="rule" id="b392-b0bd-ceb8-e3f8" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0001" />
        <infoLink name="Initiative Training" hidden="false" type="rule" id="e0a6-c2d6-e9ac-f1f0" targetId="a300-0000-0000-0003" />
      </infoLinks>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Borgward B-IV Demolition Vehicle" hidden="false" id="6b62-bd8b-569a-1049" typeId="9b00-0000-0000-0001" typeName="Army Book Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Period" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0001">M/L</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Composition / Type" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0002">7+ (armoured carrier)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Weapons" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0003">None</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Rules and options" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0004">Remote-controlled: It is assumed the vehicle operator is just outside the gaming area, operating the vehicle by remote. After giving a successful order to the Borgward B-IV, and before it moves, roll a die. On a roll of 1 the radio transmitter has lost contact with the vehicle: instead of executing the order, it simply goes Down where it is. On a roll of 2 the transmitter is malfunctioning: the Borgward B-IV makes a reverse move directly backwards instead of the order envisioned by the player controlling the vehicle. On any other roll (3-6) the Borgward B-IV acts normally. If a roll ever needs to be taken on another chart that affects the Borgward B-IV’s movement (E.g., mud, rubble snow etc), both rolls need to be taken.; Heavy charge: The heavy charge can only be used once per game, but it does indeed go off with a huge bang. In order to use the charge, the Borgward must be successfully ordered to Advance. Before moving, place a 4” template in contact with the centre of the front hull of the vehicle, then execute a reverse move straight back. After this, any model hit by the template counts as hit by a heavy howitzer, except that the Pen is +5 and that units in buildings (and the buildings themselves) suffer 4D6 hits instead.</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Army Book" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0005">p. 72</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Experience" id="d484-98fd-b1a2-c35f">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="false" id="b62b-b951-209a-59ad" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="false" id="85f9-a5e0-5f01-b04c" />
