          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Period" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0001">L</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Composition / Type" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0002">7+ (armoured carrier)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Weapons" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0003">, and the 251/17 half-track was a stop-gap measure, carrying a 20mm Flak 38. 4 versions were created for use by the Luftwaffe as well as the Heer. By the late war they were being issued to platoon command squads as extra fire support instead of the 251/10. Principal service and numbers manufactured: see 251/1 entry. Cost 60pts (Inexperienced), 75pts (Regular), 90pts (Veteran) Weapons 1 platform-mounted light autocannon with a 360-degree arc of fire</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Rules and options" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0004">Open-topped; Flak</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Army Book" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0005">p. 78</characteristic>
