        <profile name="Field Ambulance" hidden="false" id="af70-3a0b-124f-7f6e" typeId="9b00-0000-0000-0001" typeName="Army Book Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Period" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0001">E/M/L</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Composition / Type" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0002">6+ (soft-skin) Transport None. However, much like empty transports, ambulances are destroyed if they end their turn closer to enemy units than to friendly units, as described in the Bolt Action rulebook, page 145.</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Weapons" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0003">None</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Rules and options" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0004">and Platoon Selectors. Cost 38pts (Regular), 46pts (Veteran) Weapons None damage Value 6+ (soft-skin) Transport None. However, much like empty transports, ambulances are destroyed if they end their turn closer to enemy units than to friendly units, as described in the Bolt Action rulebook, page 145. Special Rules; Medical vehicle: Being in proximity of an ambulance means that any wounded soldiers nearby have a chance of being treated by a medic or stretcher bearer from amongst the crew of the ambulance. All infantry and artillery units within 6” of the vehicle count as within 6” of a medic.</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Army Book" typeId="9b01-0000-0000-0005">p. 92</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
